%---------------------------------%Cells%---------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Notebooks as Modules
Use `NotebookEvaluateAsModule` to import notebooks as reusable modules. The following rules apply:

<div class="ring ring-1 py-1 px-2 rounded mt-2">

- Initialization cells are evaluated once per notebook object
- The last Wolfram input cell is evaluated on every call and its result is exported
- All other cells are ignored
- Context of all global symbols will be completely isolated

</div>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Notebooks as Modules
Use `NotebookEvaluateAsModule` to import notebooks as reusable modules. The following rules apply:

<div class="ring ring-1 py-1 px-2 rounded mt-2">

- Initialization cells are evaluated once per notebook object
- The last Wolfram input cell is evaluated on every call and its result is exported
- All other cells are ignored
- Context of all global symbols will be completely isolated

</div>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
nb = NotebookOpen[FileNameJoin[{
  "attachments",
  "module.wln"
}], Visible->False];

{exportedSymbol} = NotebookEvaluateAsModule[nb];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Or directly

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Or directly

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
{exportedSymbol} = NotebookEvaluateAsModule[FileNameJoin[{
  "attachments",
  "module.wln"
}]];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
__We recommend to use async version__, since it breaks the evaluation order anyway

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
__We recommend to use async version__, since it breaks the evaluation order anyway

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
NotebookEvaluateAsModuleAsync[FileNameJoin[{
  "attachments",
  "module.wln"
}]]~Then~Function[result, 
  {exportedSymbol} = result
];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Now we can use it

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Now we can use it

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
exportedSymbol[]

